{
  "schema": 1,
  "id": "mov-reference-trace",
  "gate": "required",
  "operation": "mov-reference-trace",
  "candidate": "isobmff-views-worker",
  "worker_operation": "mov-trace-",
  "runner": "cargo xtask report",
  "reference": "ffmpeg-isobmff-views-native",
  "contract": [
    "Run one model with the supplied read maximum and work quantum. FFmpeg opens the same preloaded source with +noparse+nofillin and a 32768-byte custom AVIO buffer.",
    "Receiver compares track ID and public signed PTS and DTS on every packet in delivery order, including the no-timestamp bits. Initial compares the first av_read_frame return code using the rejected-seek job and the modeled packet disposition for the other outcomes. A first-read case may supply an absolute rewind anchor; the reference checks the first successful absolute seek during open and the candidate uses the same rewind.",
    "Diagnostics compares warning and error log level and message bytes in order during open. Configuration and header compare the open result and every installed extradata byte. For dOps the header job identifies the source box and its bytes are projected to the public Opus identification layout.",
    "Transport compares each data read as byte offset, requested length and return value, and each seek as whence, argument and returned offset, then the final logical position. Length inquiries do not change the physical position. The optional rewind anchor is fixed in the candidate fixture geometry and the reference determines its own seek destination.",
    "Kind 1 is a timestamp or read row, kind 2 is a byte count followed by configuration, and kind 3 is a seek row or log level and byte count followed by the message. Kinds 7 and 8 report success or refusal, with the signed return code where the model exposes one."
  ],
  "required_profiles": [
    "receiver",
    "diagnostics",
    "configuration",
    "header",
    "initial",
    "transport"
  ],
  "required_targets": [
    "aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu",
    "thumbv7neon-unknown-linux-gnueabihf"
  ],
  "iterations": 1,
  "minimum_pairs": 30,
  "confidence": 0.95,
